05:10:46 AGENT (turn 1): An llms.txt file is a plain-text (Markdown) file placed at a site's root, usually at /llms.txt. It gives an AI agent a short, curated guide to the site. It typically has a title, a one-line summary, and organized links to the most useful pages, such as docs, API references, and policies, each with a brief description. An agent doesn't have to crawl the whole site or parse cluttered HTML to work out what's there and where the important content lives. It can read this one file, pick the relevant pages, and fetch them, often as clean Markdown. That saves context window space and time, and it can make answers more accurate. It's a convention, not an enforced standard, so support varies across agents. It also guides discovery but doesn't control access the way robots.txt does.
