05:10:54 AGENT (turn 2): Your site scored 71. Two findings matter most, and both are failures.

1. **Markdown negotiation fails.** When an agent requests a page with `Accept: text/markdown`, your site returns HTML. Agents then have to parse cluttered markup, which uses more of their context window and makes errors more likely. This affects every page, and your llms.txt already points agents to the content. Fixing it would make that content easier to read.

2. **MCP discovery fails.** `/.well-known/mcp-server` returns a 404, so agents can't automatically find a tool endpoint on your site. If you run an MCP server, publish it at that path. If you don't, this matters less.

The A2A agent card warning is next. The card has no skills array, so agents can't tell what your site can do. llms.txt and the robots.txt rules for AI crawlers both pass.
