05:10:59 AGENT (turn 3): Fix markdown negotiation first. It affects every page an agent reads, and it doesn't depend on whether you run an MCP server.

The smallest change is to add one rule at your web server or CDN. When a request has `Accept: text/markdown`, it should return a Markdown copy of the page with the header `Content-Type: text/markdown`. It should also send `Vary: Accept` so caches keep the HTML and Markdown versions separate. You can start with just your most important pages, the ones your llms.txt links to. For those, put a pre-written `.md` file next to each page and have the rule serve it. You don't need to convert the whole site.

I can't see your stack, so I can't give you exact config. The rule would look different on nginx, Cloudflare, Netlify, or Vercel. If you tell me which one you use, I can be more specific.
